PROVENANCE_NOTE = """<div class="note"><strong>Evidence.</strong> No number on this board was supplied to me and none was estimated. Club rates for both seasons were computed match by match from ESPN&rsquo;s public match record &mdash; results for goals, over 2.5, BTTS, clean sheets and failed-to-score; per-match boxscores for corners, fouls, cards, shots and possession; key-event periods for first-half goals &mdash; and cross-checked against each club&rsquo;s ESPN season statistics object. Expected goals, non-penalty xG, PPDA and deep completions come from Understat for both seasons and every club. <strong>League baselines are in baselines_0918.md</strong>: the 2025&ndash;26 lines are carried unchanged from baselines_0917.md and cost no search, and the 2026&ndash;27 lines were computed the same way over every completed match of this season &mdash; 27 in the Bundesliga, 40 in Serie A, 36 in Ligue 1, 40 in the Premier League, 59 in LaLiga. The Bundesliga figures reproduce the line already in baselines_0917.md from an independent FotMob count, which is why this board trusts the method. <strong>Fields unpublished across the slate:</strong> a penalty rate for all five referees, in every source reached; ESPN&rsquo;s 2025&ndash;26 xG for any club, which is why last season&rsquo;s xG is Understat throughout; xG of any kind for Monza&rsquo;s 2025&ndash;26, because Serie B publishes none and none was modelled; fees for most of Monza&rsquo;s twelve arrivals and for Espanyol&rsquo;s six loans; any fee at all in Chelsea&rsquo;s own window review, so every Chelsea figure here is press-reported. <strong>Last season standing in for a thin current sample:</strong> nowhere in full &mdash; every strip carries both columns side by side with the match count in brackets &mdash; but the 26/27 column is three matches per club at Bayern&ndash;Union and four at the Serie A, Ligue 1 and Premier League fixtures, and should be read as such. <strong>Contradictions, and what the team sheets settled.</strong> Resolved by the confirmed lists: Friedrich and Nsoki are both out for Union and Imeri is fit; Takumi Minamino is fit and a substitute, which ends the cruciate-or-muscle dispute in the least severe direction; Jonathan Gradit is fit enough for the Lens bench; the LaLiga fixture is at the RCDE Stadium, as the fixture record said and one preview denied. Still unresolved and named on the cards: whether Chris Bedia joined or left Union; whether Paul Pogba signed for Monaco or was released by it on 19 August; Monaco&rsquo;s net transfer balance. <strong>One thing the team sheets did not resolve but corrected: Elche&rsquo;s head coach is Mart&iacute;n Anselmi, appointed 13 June 2026, not Eder Sarabia. The card said Sarabia and said he was suspended from the bench. Both were wrong.</strong> New absences the previews missed: Ansu Fati (calf) for Monaco and Yeferson Paz for Sassuolo.</div>"""

